<title>CAMEROON: Cameroon sets new cocoa/coffee export taxes.</title>
<headline>Cameroon sets new cocoa/coffee export taxes.</headline>
<dateline>YAOUNDE 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cameroon will apply cocoa and coffee export taxes of 3,500 CFA ($5.75) per tonne from around the end of August, a government statement said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>A contribution of 825 CFA a tonne to Cameroon's Interprofessional Cocoa and Coffee Council and another of 1,500 CFA a tonne to international cocoa and coffee organisations, ICCO and ICO, would also be levied.</p>
<p>Cameroon recently vowed to tackle quality problems which followed donor-sponsored liberalisation of cocoa and coffee marketing structures in the early 1990s.</p>
<p>Cameroon has said a proliferation of inexperienced exporters and buyers after 1991 was partly at the root of the problem.</p>
<p>($ = 610 CFA francs)</p>
